\description{
Mirrors the CellSweep reference implementation's defaults. The
pseudocounts (\code{celltype_lambda}, \code{ambient_lambda}, \code{bulk_lambda}) are given
on the scale you see here and divided by the gene count internally. Two of
these are worth knowing about before you touch anything else.
\code{freeze_ambient_profile = TRUE} keeps the ambient profile at its
empty-droplet estimate, which is the recommended path and the only one where
\code{alpha_cap}, the repulsion terms and cell-type reassignment are live. And
\code{freeze_empties} only accepts \code{TRUE}: the reference gives empty droplets a
cell-type component they have no label for, which indexes past the end of the
profile matrix and wraps onto the last cell type.
